A||||23||fierospeeder||Idiot Drivers||||8||
Z||000000||fierospeeder||02-07-2000||02:25 PM||||As an average jeff gordon/john force wanna be i love driving fast, but i do it safely.  I'll drive 10 over the speed limit in the suburbs because of speed traps, hey no tickets in one year.  But i will go drive fast on the highway usually the top speed my cars will go.  My fiero 4 cylinder is more then 85.  My tbird which is a 4 cylinder with a turbo can go more then 100, the dumb thing ford did was reduce 40hp on the automatics and had 190hp on the sticks because of differents cams and the stick can go 140mph, probably more with the boost up.  <P>I know you guys probably get idiots that match speeds with you.  So today, im driving in my tbird in the fast lane and theres cars in front of me driving slow, so i go into the center lane to pass them up.  While i was going to pass this one guy, floors his lincoln continental so i couldn't pass him up, and theres a suv in front of him, and i had to slow down because of cars in front of me.  Its some guy whos 40-50 yrs old with his wife and he does this same thing two times, after having to pass people, i went in the slow lane and finally passed the guy and went back on the fast lane seeing the guy atleast a mile away in my rearview mirror.  <BR>I had the samething happen when i was in my fiero, its the 2.5 so very bad in acceleration, some *****  in the fast lane speeds up and i had to slow down, because they know you want to get in front of them.  <P>Driving fast is safe unless some idiot is making it dangerous for you.  I know we have the fiero accident forum going on right now.  I havn't been in accidents but i have came close a lot of times, im at more risks getting into accidents driving the speedlimit off the highway on city streets.  People cutting you off because they think they can make it.  I came close into getting hit by a city bus because it went through the red light to make a left hand turn, while my light is green i took off in my fiero.  I know some people like suvs but lately i seen a lot of fiero owners being hit by them in this forum.  A lot of the drivers drive them wreckless going in and out of traffic as if it has .92G skid pad like a fiero.  Werent they on the news for tipping over?  <BR>I know fieros are safe in a crash but i dont want to get into one, i love my fiero and im never going to sell it.  People love to tailgate you and try to run you over in the fiero.  Near my home 5 blocks away, driving my fiero in the right lane, a van driving parellel to me in the left lane is going to switch lanes while im there, i started driving in the gravel shoulder, until the driver realized i was there and he backed off and i passed him.  Unless thats his lack of looking in his mirrors, i was in my tbird in chicago while a stationwagon is going to go into me, the same way as the van tried to, i was near his tail.  So im watching him and he tries to hit me then he backs off looks in his rearview mirror instead of looking at his side or over his shoulder and he tries again, i hit the brakes, and follow his bumper.<BR>Anyone else hate things that people do while driving, no turnsignals, stopping 2 car lengths from the car in front of them?<BR>  <BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||Cooter||02-07-2000||05:25 PM||||Around Christmas last year I was going home after work. I was in the right lane and proceded to signal to make a change to the left lane. I gave a signal, looked to make sure traffic was clear and started over. The car that was behind me punched it and tried to get into the left lane as I am already moving over. They did not give a signal or anything! I kept going and the woman started blowing her horn and flashing her lights at me. I was pissed! So, being the ****  that I am I downshifted into second, popped the clutch and stood on the brakes. She was in a nice car so I figured that she had insurance. Lucky for her, she managed to slow down and not hit me. Then she got back in the right lane and drove at least 2 miles down the road and made a right turn. I cant figure out why she had to block me, to only have to change lanes again to make her turn. IDIOTS!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula||02-07-2000||08:55 PM||||just remember that the fiero (it might just be 88s) can stop in 119 ft compared to the 200+ feet of a normal suv. So I wouldn't slam on the brakes in front of people.<P>I can see why people stop 1 or 2 car lengths away at stoplights because if you get rearended and hit the car in front of you, ITS YOUR FAULT FOR HITTING THE FRONT CAR.  It doesn't matter that you were just hit from behind.<P>and more people can see your low roofline if you arent directly behind a big suv/truck.<P>I almost got hit by a schoolbus in the school parking lot because the idiot didn't look behind the bus and started going in reverse through the intersection.  I was stopped at a stopsign trying to get through.  Anyways I had to punch the ol' V6 to make get away.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||02-07-2000||09:12 PM||||Formula, I usually dont do the "brake check", this was a rare incident. I have never heard that if you get rear ended and knocked into another car that it was your fault. In Alabama, that is not true. I know because my sister got knocked into another car at a red light and the guy that hit her had to pay for both cars. Maybe it is finally good to live in 'Bama! Well, then again- maybe not.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierospeeder||02-07-2000||11:40 PM||||I got my automatic and i shift it into 1 or 2 so i have engine braking.  I try not to brake at all but probably the person thats tailgating me is.  <P>You know your getting followed by a kewl driver if they are giving you space and you know they drive like you.  I do the same also, there was some hot chick in a a camaro and we are going in and out of traffic, i use turn signals all the time, but you see some moron in his honda tailgating you when its 20mph traffic and your wondering whats his point.<P>I wish people had more highway respect also, if they see a fast car they should move to the right lane and move back if they wish.  About 50% of people do that even.  Unlike today. <P> I also hate that im going 90 and this chick in a Jeep cherokee which i totally hate SUV poseur, people commuting in a large vehicle alone, i wonder if she goes offroading?  Im going 90 and im about 4 or 5 car lenghs away while sees in the middle lane.  Instead of letting me go by she gets in my lane because i guess the vehicle in her lane was going to slow.  I had to slam on my brakes because shes going 30mph slower.  I tailgated her ass, and she kept on looking at her side mirror seeing my tbird on her ass and she finally speed up and changed lanes to the middle and went back to the fast lane.  I know it was safe to tailgate her because there was nothing in front of me at the time i was speeding.  Unless shes those people that hit her brakes for no particular reason which i have seen people doing with no one around them.<P>1pt for cooter||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierospeeder||02-08-2000||12:01 AM||||But isn't there a limit on how far you should stop behind another car?  two car lengths is kind of out of the question.  I know in illinois you can get a ticket for following closly but i havn't heard about getting a ticket for stopping closly.  Even if you parked two car lengths, and a semi smacks you, that momentum is going to make you hit that car in front. <P>My moms friend's daughter was driving her fathers new i think chevy silverado &lt;drool&gt;  no suv, and she stopped suddenly in traffic i have no idea why, but three people ran into each other people, they were tailgating and they all got tickets. You caused an accident because you followed to closely and was unable to stop.  <P>Ive been in a situation similar, but no accident.  This is going to school in chicago, college.  Driving on historic route 66, and its heavy traffic.  There is a railroad bridge about 6 car lengths long, and two car lanes on each side.  On the other side of the bridge there is a alley you can turn into which you can only access turning left in the left lane.  <BR>Everyings bumper to bumper about 20 to 30 mph and i guess three cars down someone didn't signal or just stopped so they can turn left, and people are assuming that traffic isn't going to stop.  The first three cars slam on their brakes suddenly and i hit mine, while im under the bridge i hear about 3 skids saying oh shit thinking theres going to be a pile up.  Glad the people behind me and the ones behind them stopped on time.<P>I was comming back from dropping my girlfriend off which my mom doesn't really like because she has a kid from another guy.  "you can do better son"  while driving back from greenbay wisconsin, im in chicago driving on I-90 and its getting dark.  Its a three lane highway with psychotic drivers from chicago.  Suddenly i see all these red lights in front of me, thinking oh shoot traffic, which is common on this highway.  The cars start moving but very slowly, i see im behind a car and i guess it stalled or something.  I slowly drive around and it looks like a nascar wreck with about 4 cars that hit each other, under a bridge.  I remember seeing this one lady who i think hit the car in front of her but her cars end was up in the air on top of another cars hood and i saw her face as she was looking back of her car wondering why is her car in an incline.   I thought to myself that i might have been in this wreck if i was 2 or 3 seconds quicker.<P>I guess highways are not that safe even if everyone drives the same direction!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||02-08-2000||03:17 AM||||Around here, nobody stops 1-2 car lenghts away at stoplights.  Everybodies on each others bumbers.  Lots of tailgaters, too.  I've learned that if you see somebody zooming up behind you in your rearview, wait till they get kinda close and then tap your brakes.  They slow down quick.  Did that on some ***** in a Cherokee.  why are the worst drivers always driving jeeps?  I've been known to do a brake check sometimes, and now that I have a v6 I might actually be able to pass someone on the highway...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Shiner||02-08-2000||04:07 AM||||I hate it when people get right up your a$$ at a stoplight or stop sign on a hill.  I have to take off like a funny car to keep from rolling back that 5" or whatever they leave behind me!  Of course, I don't think they even considered that the person in front of them was driving a manual trans.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Patrick||02-08-2000||04:24 AM||||<BR>In regards to tailgaters, I've always thought that it would be an interesting idea to hook up a toggle switch on the dash for the brake lights. Then you could simply flick the switch (as you continue to drive full speed) and watch in your rear view mirror as the b*st*rd behind you goes all squirrely jumping on his brakes.||||reg||10
