Z||000010||lennyb4||02-08-2000||09:14 AM||||Thats o.k. I was sitting at a red light about two weeks ago (3pm clear day) and got clipped by a lady in a SUV. She was talking on her car phone and said my car is so small she didnt even see me. Now my fiero is candy apple red W/metalflake in it. How cant you see it? Now i have to replace my rear facia, tail light, deck lid. etc.. And shes even trying to fight it in court. Some people just p**s me off. It seems like SUV owners believe that they own the roads. At least in northern Ohio. Oh well Sh*t happens and i love my car to much not to fix it.||||reg||8
Z||000011||DJRice||02-08-2000||09:14 AM||||Be glad you dont have to drive in Orlando, FL.  The land of tourists who are forever unsure of where exactly they are and where they want to be....<P>I call them the "Hey dad look, they have Mickey Mouse T-shirts 3 for $10" maneuvers.||||reg||1
Z||000012||SpeedPhreak||02-08-2000||12:03 PM||||cell phones really pi$$ me off. bad.  i cant stand them suv/big haired/afraid to get your hands dirty/stuck up/snotty/....man i can go on for ever. <P>riding a motorcycle for more miles than i put on cars has taught me that there are so many idiots the active driver w/common sense & an idea of there surrounding is a very rare thing.  i have learned to anticipate actions of drivers by what they are driving, traffic conditions, & when i get close enough their apperance.  ie, my brother & i were behind this car (like an old escort) that was doing like 10 under... he was getting mad so was i.  we came up to a stop sign to turn right on to a 4 lane road (2 eachway) all the traffic was in the left lane... instead of turning into the right lane like she was supposed to do we waited like a minute for traffic to clear...i told my brother that she would turn into the left lane & we could pass her on the right (i told him this before we even came to a complete stop)...well it happened just like i said. <P>the moral of the story... be an active driver & with time you should be a road way prophet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>ps, did u know that people who travel 10mph under the speed limit cause &/or involved in more accidents than people who travel 10+over!?!  mmmm.... damn the man & his speedtraps.||||reg||1
Z||000013||DRH||02-08-2000||12:13 PM||||Riding a motorcycle will definitely enhance your defensive driving skills. You learn to assume every car coming out a side road with a stop sign will look right at you then pull out anyway!!! (or turn left in your path, or force you out of your lane, or ???)||||reg||1
Z||000014||Eric||02-08-2000||07:17 PM||||Slow drivers are the worst.  I hate it when the flow of traffic is ten over and the guy in front of me is going ten under.  At that point it gets hard to merge into the fast lane.  A driver without my skills/experience/reflexes could cause a wreck when they tried to overtake the slower car.<P>As I was driving down a two lane country road the other day (hilly road with no centerline), I approached a blind hill.  I couldn't see if any traffic was coming the other direction so I got over as far right as I could without hitting the snow bank.  Just as I get to the crest, BWAWAWAWAW a school bus with a full load of kids comes barreling down the CENTER of the road.  I was only going about 20mph but this bus was doing atleast 45.  I just closed my eyes and waited for it to be over.  I seriously thought something was going to happen.  Looked up and realized I was still alive when I heard the faint tone of a bus horn directly behind me.  I was so shaken up, I didn't even think to turn around and get the bus#.  I really regret that just thinking of all those kids who could have ended up down in the ditch after the bus ramped my car.  Imagine if my car was a dump truck or even an Suv, you guys would have been hearing about this on the national news.  Now that I think about it, maybe I should call up the school and ask which bus goes that direction in the morning and tell them what I'm telling you.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Patrick||02-08-2000||07:21 PM||||<BR>Do it.||||reg||4
Z||000016||olympic||02-08-2000||08:21 PM||||  Has anyone heard of the new car called the Dislexus.  When you signal left it turns right.  They sell alot of them around here.  They also sell alot of accelerator delete cars in my town. Aout 50% of the residents where I live are seniors and they all just about drive me insane.  They put there Grand Marquis and Chevy Trucks in gear and idle them around town.  I've followed countless Blue haired old ladies clear across town doing 10 mph or less!!!  ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Standard||02-09-2000||03:29 AM||||Patrick -- <P>My 84 is kind of like that.. my brake pedal has some play, i can push it down a little and it'll light up the brake lights but it won't slow me down any.  it rules.  I should get around to bleeding my brakes sometime, tho.. Oh well.. i'm too busy playing with my GT now.||||reg||6
Z||000018||fierospeeder||02-09-2000||11:31 PM||||I know all my cars have that play, you just very slightly touch the brakes, and you hear the switch turn on for the taillights without you slowing down.<BR>I see people driving while their foot is on the brake.  The problem is when they stop at a light its red and when they start accelerating their brake lights are still on.  Atleast its a little better then the people that have no taillights at all.||||reg||1
Z||000019||87GTBro||02-10-2000||01:06 AM||||If there are any elderly people reading this, please don't take any offense.<P>Down where I live in Texas, winter is the worst driving season of the year.  Not because of snow or ice, but because of Winter Texans.  These are all old retired folks that live up in the northern states during the spring, summer and fall and come down to live in Texas for the winter months.<P>None of them know how to drive!!!  I guess Driver's ED didn't exist 80 years ago, but experience should teach you just as much.  Wouldn't it make sense that if there is a stop sign, you need to stop and if their isn't a stop sign, you shouldn't stop in the middle of the street?<P>This happened just tonight.  My brother and I were driving to the local Pep Boys Auto Parts store and we were going under an overpass to turn left to get on the highway.  Well, the oncoming traffic has a stop sign (There are no traffic lights at this intersection)  There is no stop sign on our side.  You just pull up to the intersection and continue left.  No yield sign or anything.  Go and turn.  Anyway, this evening as we were making that turn, there was a huge Lincoln there.  First he was in the other lane, then he moved over to the turn lane at about 3 miles per hour.  By the time our vehicle reached his, he decided he wanted to stop and wait for the oncoming traffic at the stop sign.  (The Winter Texan was from Iowa)  So we lay on the horn (They must think Texans are rude!)  But finally the guy starts going and looking at us like we did something wrong.  Hello!!!  I could have plowed right into the back of him.  He could have caused an accident by stopping in the middle of the road.  <P>I think Senior Citizens should have to take State conducted driving tests once every two years or so.  Keep the dangerous people off the road.  It will keep everyone safer.<P>||||reg||12
Z||000020||DaRkLoRD||02-10-2000||01:25 AM||||87GTBro, it's no better up here in Canada.<P>There's a stopsign less than 75' from my house, perpendicular to my street. No one.. I mean NO ONE stops there unless someone's crossing the street or a car is driving down my street. Even then people don't always stop. Back in the summer I saw a pickup truck going way over the limit (40kph in town) and it went right through the stop sign.. but the worst part is, <B>a lady was crossing the road with a stroller!</B> the truck almost ran over the stroller, but the lady was able to yank it out of the way in time. And he didn't even slow down.<P>I occasionally even see cops run stopsigns here.. not going anywhere, just driving around. they slow down to about 10kph, but most people don't stop.<P>I never claimed to be a perfect driver, but if I ever did anything that stupid, I'd turn in my own license before someone got hurt. <BR>I've been in a few close calls, but nothing really serious. I really hate it when people try to go through a stop sign and then slam on the brakes and lay on the horn when you cross the road in front of them.. I've been tempted to walk up to the window and start freaking on them, and maybe explain the concept of a "STOP" sign, as opposed to the "SLOW DOWN BUT KEEP GOING" sign they seem to see instead...<p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 02-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||fierospeeder||02-10-2000||12:56 PM||||Here in illinois, a few times a year.  The senior citizens are known to hit the gas pedal instead of the brake.  The results are them on the news by several channels.  I remember one in downtown that she went of a parking garage and slammed into a building.||||reg||1
Z||000022||wkayl||02-10-2000||03:05 PM||||One of these days when that guy (or gal) stops so close to my GT that I can't even see their headlights i'm going to get out and tell them that my car runs just fine and I don't need a push.  I just hope they take it as a joke and don't shoot me.||||reg||1
Z||000023||Formula||02-10-2000||04:25 PM||||some lady in pittsburgh drove right through the hole in one of the parking garages (renovations "caution" tape instead of cement) and fell 2 or 3 stories straight down onto the sidewalk and was fine. (the car wasn't though)||||reg||1
